The following is instructions on running the corrisponding code.
The code can be can from JupyterLab or any environment that can handle python code. 
It is highly recommend to install CUDA drivers with the following command:

pip install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121

Then run the following command to ensure your CUDA enable graphics card has been found. 

import torch
print(torch.cuda.is_available())  # Should return True
print(torch.cuda.get_device_name(0) if torch.cuda.is_available() else "No CUDA device")

If you do not have a CUDA enable GPU please turn down sample size and hidden layer size or the training of the model will take a long time. Epochs can also be reduced but will reduce accuracy on some models outcomes. 
